"""Walk-through of lesson 40, Design a Chat System.

Example numbers (mine, checked by script; they follow the section text): 50 million daily users x 40 messages = 2 billion a day = about 23,000 a second;
200 bytes each = 400 GB a day = about 150 TB a year. 20 million sockets at peak / 200,000 per gateway = 100 gateways.
Registry entry TTL 60 s, heartbeat every 20 s. Conversation 88: the next sequence number is 42; a reconnecting app has 41.
A group of 200 with 120 online: 1 store + 120 deliveries. Presence: 20 million people x 4 sessions a day x 2 changes = 160 million changes a day = 1,852 a second;
x 200 contacts = 370,000 updates a second; x 20 who have the chat open = 37,000. A gateway dies: 200,000 sockets / 99 gateways = 2,020 each in one second;
with jitter over 30 s: 6,667 a second in all, 67 per gateway.
"""
